\id TST Test Bible Book
\ide UTF-8
\h Test Book
\toc1 The Book of Tests
\mt1 Test Book
\c 1
\s First Section
\p
\v 1 In the beginning there was a test.
\v 2 And the test was good.
\v 3 Then came \qt a quoted phrase\qt* within a verse.
\p
\v 4 This verse has a \f + footnote that should be excluded\f*footnote nearby.
\v 5-6 This is a verse range spanning two verses.
\c 2
\s Poetry Section
\p
\v 1 A normal paragraph to start.
\q1
\v 2 This is a line of poetry,
\q2 and it continues on a second line.
\q1
\v 3 Another poetic verse,
\q2 with a nested \qt \add deeply nested\add* quote\qt* element.
\p
\v 4 Back to normal prose.
\c 3
\s Continuation Test
\p
\v 1 First verse of chapter three.
\p Continuation text for verse one.
\v 2 Second verse starts here.
